    "summary": "Epic Dark Star suite, gritty Row Jimmy, tight rhythm throughout",
    "blurb": "The show shines with an unforgettable Dark Star → Eyes Of The World → China Doll sequence, complemented by a fiery Row Jimmy and solid Playing In The Band. Jerry’s down‑and‑dirty lead guitar and Phil’s booming bass drive the second set, while Keith provides crisp piano throughout.",
    "review": "On February 15, 1973 at Dane County Coliseum, the Dead delivered one of their quintessential early‑’73 performances. The first set roared through a punchy mix of folk‑rock staples—Loose Lucy, Beat It On Down The Line, and a seamless China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider transition—setting up a high‑energy launch into Row Jimmy, where Jerry’s gritty lead cut through with soaring solos. \n\nThe second set is the show’s crown jewel: a monumental Dark Star → Eyes Of The World → China Doll suite that reviewers call “epic” and “masterpiece,” featuring Phil’s juicy bass solo and Bill’s crisp tom work. Here Comes Sunshine, El Paso, and a tight Playing In The Band keep the momentum rolling into a joyous encore of Uncle John’s Band and One More Saturday Night. Keith’s piano is a perfect accompaniment throughout, and Donna’s backing vocals add extra sparkle. For anyone chasing that classic 1973 magic, this show delivers it in spades.",
